+   non-overlapping ranges over 6 interleaved `perf` rounds. So the S-X8 fix is the tile decode, as
+   briefed — but **WI-1724 is not dead**: q8_0 wants those pipelines.
+2. **The decode fix is a TIE on this shape, not a win.** `perf` mode (22-30 dispatches averaged, the
+   brief's instrument) reads **-1.18% median with overlapping ranges**. An earlier single-dispatch
+   reading of -2.20% is **SUPERSEDED and withdrawn** — see §4.1. The switch ships default-ON on the
+   distributable-engine ground (strictly fewer ops, bit-identical result), **not on a measured gain**.
+3. **The brief's premise does not hold at this shape.** S-X8 `mul_mm` is **15.3% FASTER than q8_0**
+   here (35169 vs 41511 us). The R48i 4B pp128 deficit is real but its cause is **not** the
+   27B-class prefill `mul_mm` shape; it is still open.
+4. **The coverage hole is the lane's most durable finding** — see §1. Nothing in this tree, in either
+   mode, had ever exercised the S-X8 `mul_mm` tile decode at a width `mul_mm` actually runs at.
 
